# {{ s.name }} — Waypoint Marker

**Variant:** {{ variant }}

{{ s.description }}

## What it does

`{{ s.name }}` builds one small on-screen marker at `Awake()` (finding or
creating a `Canvas` the same way `SceneSetup` does) and, every `LateUpdate()`,
clamps it to the screen edge in the direction of whatever target `SetTarget`
last named. It hides itself when there is no target, the target hasn't
spawned yet, the target is already fully on-screen, or the player is within
3 world units of it.

## API

```csharp
var waypoint = GameContext.Instance.Get<{{ s.name }}>();
waypoint.SetTarget("VaultDoor");   // points at the spawned "VaultDoor_0"
waypoint.SetTarget("");           // hides the marker
```

## Wiring

Composed alongside the "objectives" subsystem (`unity_compose.subsystems_for`)
whenever a mission has real objectives in a spatial (non-board) project. The
generated `GameWiring.RefreshObjectiveHud()` calls `SetTarget` with the same
`targetRef` its HUD text reads — the marker and the HUD label always name the
same objective.
